May 25th - I almost finished the basic hardware part of PipeBot FPV and started working on the coding section.

Today I tested the ESP32 WiFi control idea, where the ESP32 creates its own WiFi network and opens a webpage for controlling the robot. I also started adding forward, backward, left, right, and stop controls for the motor driver.

The current prototype is still basic, but now the project is moving from just hardware assembly into actual control and testing. Next I will test the motors with the L298N driver, improve the wiring, and document the camera setup.
